      "id": "7241000000000000002",
      "num_comments": 35,
      "num_likes": 307,
      "num_shares": 15,
      "post_text": "A creator brief does not cost what you pay the creator. We tracked eleven of them: median fee $340, median true cost $1,180, median wait eleven days. The gap is briefs, notes, licensing questions and the seasonal angle expiring while you wait.",
      "post_type": "post",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/vidora_activity-7241000000000000002",
      "user_followers": 18400,
      "user_id": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/vidora"
    },
    "source_id": "7241000000000000002"
  },
  {
    "payload": {
      "_competitor_ref": "vidora.ai",
      "date_posted": "2026-07-17T09:05:00.000Z",
      "hashtags": [
        "#vidora",
        "#ugc"
      ],
      "id": "7241000000000000001",
      "num_comments": 19,
      "num_likes": 214,
      "num_shares": 9,
      "post_text": "We gave one product page to Vidora and asked for thirty ads before dinner. Twenty-eight were forgettable. Two carried the month. That ratio is the whole argument for volume, and it only works when a forgettable ad costs four minutes instead of a shoot.",
      "post_type": "post",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/vidora_activity-7241000000000000001",
      "user_followers": 18400,
      "user_id": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/vidora"
